        "original_id": "94e0f10b-26d4-5f7e-919a-440b3333c66a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sault Ste. Marie, Michigan; New York, United States\n- Projects: Edison Sault Power Canal; Cayuga–Seneca Canal\n- Organizations: Cloverland Electric Cooperative; New York State Canal System\n- Products: Saint Marys Falls Hydropower Plant\n- Events: Historic Civil Engineering Landmark designation\n\nFacts:\n- Excavation of the Edison Sault Power Canal began in September 1898 and was completed in June 1902.\n- The Edison Sault Power Canal supplies the Saint Marys Falls Hydropower Plant in Sault Ste. Marie, Michigan.\n- The Saint Marys Falls Hydropower Plant is a Cloverland Electric Cooperative hydroelectric plant.\n- The Edison Sault Power Canal and its hydroelectric complex were named a Historic Civil Engineering Landmark in 1983.\n- The Cayuga–Seneca Canal is a canal in New York, United States.\n- The Cayuga–Seneca Canal is now part of the New York State Canal System.",
